 the position of rele- vant information; §4.1) use a bidirectional encoder to contextualize input contexts—can we use this observation to improve decoder-only mod- els by placing the query before and after the data, enabling query-aware contextualization of documents (or key-value pairs)? We find that query-aware contextualization dra- matically improves performance on the key-value retrieval task—all models achieve near-perfect performance on the 75, 140, and 300 key-value pair settings. For example, GPT-3.5-Turbo (16K) with query-aware contextualization achieves per- fect performance when evaluated with 300 key-value pairs. In contrast, without query-aware contextual- ization, the worst-case performance is 45.6% (Figure 7). Despite the significant impact on key-value retrieval performance, query-aware contextualization minimally affects performance trends in the multi-document question"
