dy yields a good Embeddoc function. However, it is possible that refreshing the in- dex would further improve performance. 3.4. Injecting inductive biases into pre-training In the process of developing REALM, we discovered sev- eral additional strategies that further guide the model to- wards meaningful retrievals, described below. Salient span masking During REALM pre-training, we want to focus on examples x that require world knowledge to predict the masked tokens. As explained in Section 2, some MLM spans only require local context. To focus on problems that require world knowledge, we mask salient spans such as “United Kingdom” or “July 1969”. We use a BERT-based tagger trained on CoNLL-2003 data (Sang & De Meulder, 2003) to identify named entities, and a"
